# Hobb, ashore at the Keel, with a new arm to show.
dialogue hobb4
  node root hobb "Clerk. …Started the other arm."
    > "Who's on it?" -> who
    > "Goodnight, Hobb." -> bye
  node who hobb "Tam."
    -> holds
  node holds narrator "He holds it out. One name, and a great deal of skin."
    -> room
  node room hobb "That one's for the ones that come back. There's room."
    > "Put me on it." -> me
    > "There's a lot of room." -> lot
  node me hobb "Don't rush me. Come back a few more times. Then we'll talk ink."
  node lot hobb "Good."
  node bye hobb "Mind the step. There isn't one. I just like saying it now."
  node again hobb "Still room, clerk. I check."
